<lesson id="les-l9-01-ring-cut" title="Close the provincial ring" level="9" minutes="15" goal="Any single backbone cable can break and PopPalu still reaches SulawesiContent"/>
<step n="1" text="Five backbone POPs circle the province, but the cable between PopManado and PopMakassar is plugged in with both ports turned off. The ring is really a line."/>
<step n="2" text="On PopManado, turn port GigabitEthernet0/1 on. Do the same for GigabitEthernet0/1 on PopMakassar. The ring closes and OSPF learns the second way around."/>
<step n="3" text="Break the Makassar side in your head: if the PopMakassar to PopParepare cable is cut, traffic must travel the long way around the ring." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="Now the middle: a cut between PopParepare and PopPalu must also heal." check="c2"/>
<step n="5" text="And the cable you just brought up may break too." check="c3"/>
<step n="6" text="The long way around is allowed to be slower, but the far POP must stay under 30 milliseconds from the content server." check="c4"/>
<check id="c1" kind="outage" from="pop3" to="server0" url="pop1:GigabitEthernet0/0" expect="ok" label="PopPalu still reaches SulawesiContent with the PopMakassar to PopParepare cable cut"/>
<check id="c2" kind="outage" from="pop3" to="server0" url="pop2:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="PopPalu still reaches SulawesiContent with the PopParepare to PopPalu cable cut"/>
<check id="c3" kind="outage" from="pop3" to="server0" url="pop5:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="PopPalu still reaches SulawesiContent with the PopManado to PopMakassar cable cut"/>
<check id="c4" kind="latency" from="pop3" to="server0" url="" expect="30" label="PopPalu reaches SulawesiContent in under 30 milliseconds"/>
